{"question":"What causal mechanisms remain credible for Attempt 3 after inspecting the champion, real-tender corpus, and evaluated experiment history?","findings":"The champion retrieves the raw line plus at most one canonical alternate, collapses raw/canonical hits to the best rank within each modality, RRF-fuses dense and BM25, and gives only the untouched raw line to DeepSeek for final selection. In the reconstructed 130-row review set, 48 are ball-valve requests, 45 contain threaded/inch cues, 43 contain third-party brand/model cues, 33 concern filters/water treatment, and 20 contain work-action wording. The LD CSV has no IVR, VALTEC, cartridge/ЭФГ, or water-treatment terms. Of the 20 action rows, some explicitly name a valve or filter product, so action wording alone is not a safe abstention signal.\n\nThe local, nearby retrieval space is now substantially saturated: endpoint/inch expansion, vendor-token suppression, manufacturer-fact enrichment, quantity-boundary repair, and variant-aware fusion all had neutral or unsafe end-to-end results. The latter two are especially important because code confirms their premises, but their evaluated changes still increased wrong-NOT_FOUND or failed public safety. Evidence supports investigating request granularity and catalog-scope uncertainty rather than another lexical or fusion refinement.","decision_impact":"The central uncertainty is whether unresolved tender value is mostly recoverable product evidence obscured by mixed service/product line items, or honest catalog-scope uncertainty for requests outside LD’s sellable taxonomy. The next experiment should discriminate those explanations while preserving raw retrieval and avoiding a forced MATCHED/NOT_FOUND decision. There is insufficient evidence for another nearby branded-model, endpoint/inch, canonicalization, parser, or query-variant-fusion refinement.","unresolved":"The review pool is unresolved, so category prevalence is not proof of end-to-end uplift. Lexical absence from the catalog is supporting evidence rather than proof of product absence; any scope mechanism needs affirmative taxonomy/category evidence and a fail-open path. The supplied review-pool gzip remains unreadable locally, but its 130 members are exactly reconstructable from the intact full corpus minus the 90 labels and 33 provisional cases.","sources":[],"evidence_patterns":[{"pattern":"Semantics-preserving retrieval changes have a narrow success boundary; semantic completion and alternate-ranking changes have not safely improved end-to-end outcomes.","supporting_experiments":["Legacy cycles 3–4 accepted additive canonicalization.","Legacy cycles 6, 9, and 17 rejected flanged, standard-bore, and actuation semantic expansions.","Attempt 1 query_evidence_preservation improved public known-positive hit rate but raised hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND by 0.08.","Attempt 2 query_variant_evidence_fusion raised public wrong-NOT_FOUND by 0.04."],"interpretation":"The code confirms that canonical variants are currently collapsed before RRF, and that a quantity-boundary defect exists. But both a repair of that defect and preservation of variant provenance have already been scientifically evaluated without safe end-to-end value. These are not credible nearby repeats absent new causal evidence.","confidence":0.97},{"pattern":"Genericizing third-party nomenclature or importing external product facts repeatedly harms abstention safety.","supporting_experiments":["Attempt 1 threaded/inch alias expansion: hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND +0.04.","Attempt 2 supplier/model-noise suppression: hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND +0.04.","Attempt 3 trusted manufacturer/model enrichment: hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND +0.08.","Review corpus: 43 branded/model-like rows; catalog lexical scan: no IVR or VALTEC tokens."],"interpretation":"Branded nomenclature is a real lexical mismatch, but the repeated failure signature indicates that source-product facts and generic wording do not establish an appropriate LD equivalent. Th